<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys two 38,000/T Mar fuel oil at $135-138.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys two 38,000/T Mar fuel oil at $135-138.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) bought two 38,000-tonne cargoes of 0.5 percent sulphur fuel oil for March delivery at $135-138 per tonne, a company official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The low pour cargo was awarded at $135-$136 per tonne for delivery on March 1-15 while the high pour cargo was awarded at $138 per tonne for March 5-15 arrival.</p>
<p>Both cargoes were awarded on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to Keelung or Taichung.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC bought two 38,000-tonne cargoes at between $136-$138 per tonne c-and-f.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-870-3571)</p>
</text>
